"""Numeral two and "second".

This component responds to the number two, written as a glyph, and to words about
the second (the ordinal "second", "twenty", "binary"). It does not respond to the
spelled-out word "two", nor to other digits.

How strong it is on a plain digit "2" depends on what comes before it:
- at the very start of a document, a lone "2" is very strong (2.5);
- right after another digit (the 2 in "12" or "2017") it is nearly off (0.1);
- right after a dot, comma or caret it is weaker (0.3);
- after a space, a letter or a symbol such as "/", "(" or "-" it is about 0.6.

Other glyphs for two (², ₂, ２, and the Chinese 二 / 贰) are about 0.8-1.0.
Words "second", "secondary" and "twenty" are about 0.85; "seconds" is weaker
(0.3). "binary", "February" and "Tuesday" (the second month and day) are about 0.5.
Everything else is 0.
